cements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T02:58:49-07:00","id":1487563,"title":"","content":"Ankla Hotep, since my very first chronicle was based on the shenanigans that surrounded him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T05:41:14-07:00","id":1487570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1487559#post1487559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lazarus. I've always liked the dude. He's one of the biggest players in the Jyhad and he's done a lot. Embraced Lamia, escaped possible destruction by refusing to follow Cappadocius, killed his older sibling, spent years studying the secrets of the Setites and the Cult of Isis, became the Capuchin, helped the Harbringers &quot;escape&quot; the Underworld, brought all the various bloodlines of the Cappadocians together, munched down on Giovanni, and apparently he's got some pretty nasty plans in store for the Hecata, maybe everyone. I expect we'll end up with him being a central figure in the near future of V5's metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lazarus definitely has the renegade / outsider appeal going on to a considerable degree for him. Also he is a renegade of a group that is already on the periphery, so it is almost as if it counts double.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-23-2022, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T08:52:02-07:00","id":1487597,"title":"","content":"I find myself liking folks like Hesha Rudhze of The Followers Of Set the most with The Dracon, Polina from the Dark Ages Lasombra Clan and Tyler from Brujah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:08:01-07:00","id":1487599,"title":"","content":"Lodin and Nicolai from CbN","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T15:52:47-07:00","id":1487658,"title":"","content":"Etrius, Tremere, Saulot, Lazarus.<br /> <br /> I hate Ur-Shulgi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T07:53:56-07:00","id":1487729,"title":"","content":"Maximillian Strauss, who happens to be my character's sire and mentor in my current game. <br /> <br /> He is portrayed as a master of politics and grandmaster of Chess, who is exceedingly subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:44:09-07:00","id":1487909,"title":"","content":"Rutor from The Red Sign. A blast to write.I am also fond of Themistocles from the same book<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:46:29-07:00","id":1487924,"title":"","content":"I can't say I have an all time favorite. I am not a fan of the signature characters although some are certainly fine concepts. Most of the By Night books after Chicago are simply terrible with either generic NPCs, characters who are obviously a former PC of the writer or one of his friends, or NPCs that terribly clash with the city they are in.<br /> <br /> I won't mention any characters from CbN because they're too well known. That the World of Darkness has basically pimped out this book THREE times is a testament to the strength of its character concepts (though not their character sheets).<br /> <br /> But out of the rest, there are a few gems in the dreck. More for their potential than how they were used in their books. <br /> <br /> One of these is the Ventrue Upton Rowlands in Dark Colony. As written, he's founding stock of New England with strong ties to Connecticut politics and business and Yale. He's from a line of Ventrue that embrace within the family. He's a Prince of two towns, and leader of the Gemini League, an undeveloped coterie based in a local social club whose main attribute is an interesting name. All good stuff, but not put to much good use in the dog's breakfast that is Dark Colony, a very poor By Night book that has a few good things in it.<br /> <br /> But so much potential! A Ventrue from American Revolutionary stock, New England old money, and who controls Yale University? How can you have this guy not be involved with Skulls &amp; Bones secret society! This guy should be the vampire symbol of the Eastern Establishment, wielding vast influence. There should be other vampire Rowlands either descended from him, or through his own sire (Aunt Georgia) scattered over the country. His control over Skull &amp; Bones should mean indirect control through that entire network of highly placed Yale graduates throughout business and government. He is the leader of all the Ventrue in the New England area and controls their collective action through his leadership of the Gemini League. He has his own spy network ferreting out threats to the regional Ventrue.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Ventrue Board of Directors for the entire North American continent, this guy should be sitting there along with Horatio Ballard making the major decisions.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LbbxQqKXUIk\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LbbxQqKXUIk\" data-code=\"LbbxQqKXUIk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LbbxQqKXUIk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This is a character that should be more prominent, but neglected because of where he was originally published.<br /> <br /> There's certainly a few others out there that are sadly neglected, but have great potential. If one of them comes to mind, I'll post again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T04:31:54-07:00","id":1488003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1487561#post1487561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could also say the ones you just like from reading.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I'd say my favourite is Sunow' from Descendants of the Three Sisters for V20. She's a very different and interesting take on a Sabbat Archbishop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T12:44:03-07:00","id":1488198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1487658#post1487658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etrius, Tremere, Saulot, Lazarus.<br /> <br /> I hate Ur-Shulgi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to many like this character. But then he was meant to be something of a disposable character to serve the metaplot that was going to end the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T12:57:28-07:00","id":1488200,"title":"","content":"Righteous Endeavor. <br /> <br /> The answer is always Righteous Endeavor, the witch hunter/witch who apparently never goes without his Pilgrim's hat, even in the modern nights. A Tzimisce NOT known for Viisscitude, cross-dressing, or embracing Nazis (although I wouldn't put it <i>past</i> him to do that last part). <br /> <br /> Triglav would have been an interesting one to have made it to the modern nights, if only to see just how problematic that would be. He probably makes Sascha Vykos (let alone Righteous Endeavor) look inconspicuous in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T15:24:50-07:00","id":1488218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488198#post1488198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to many like this character. But then he was meant to be something of a disposable character to serve the metaplot that was going to end the series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was a missed opportunity not to have Ur-Shulgi be the guys the Second Inquisition blows up instead of Vienna.<br /> <br /> As much as I defend the Tremere strike, I would have probably had the Vienna chantry just vanish one day.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was Kupala or Saulot.<br /> <br /> Whereas bombing Alamut in the middle of a war zone seems like it would be more plausible and probably done with heavy ordinance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488200#post1488200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Righteous Endeavor.<br /> <br /> The answer is always Righteous Endeavor, the witch hunter/witch who apparently never goes without his Pilgrim's hat, even in the modern nights.<b> A Tzimisce NOT known for Viisscitude, cross-dressing, or embracing Nazis (although I wouldn't put it <i>past</i> him to do that last part).</b><br /> <br /> Triglav would have been an interesting one to have made it to the modern nights, if only to see just how problematic that would be. He probably makes Sascha Vykos (let alone Righteous Endeavor) look inconspicuous in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to how much Eastern European gamers get annoyed with the tzimisce as &quot;their&quot; Clan, I note trans gamers have an issue with the philosophy of sculpting your body to perfection and the utility of Vicissitude as a sign of PURE EVIL.<br /> <br /> Which notably even gets called out in Chicago by Night.<br /> <br /> A LOT of vampires, I imagine, would love that Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-27-2022, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T16:38:26-07:00","id":1488224,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Unfortunately, the pterodactyl guy didn't want to cure cancer, he just wanted to turn people into dinosaurs.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T17:41:08-07:00","id":1488230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488218#post1488218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was a missed opportunity not to have Ur-Shulgi be the guys the Second Inquisition blows up instead of Vienna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any time you don't kill Ur-Shulgi is a missed opportunity. And yeah, bombing Alamut would be more plausible from any perspective whatsoever, could be done with heavier ordinance and less of a hassle, would be more fun and no one would give a fuck.<br /> <br /> He is a strong candidate for Most Disliked Character, and we have Sam Height in the contest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T17:45:34-07:00","id":1488231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488224#post1488224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Unfortunately, the pterodactyl guy didn't want to cure cancer, he just wanted to turn people into dinosaurs.</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>+! comic reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488230#post1488230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time you don't kill Ur-Shulgi is a missed opportunity. And yeah, bombing Alamut would be more plausible from any perspective whatsoever, could be done with heavier ordinance and less of a hassle, would be more fun and no one would give a fuck.<br /> He is a strong candidate for Most Disliked Character, and we have Sam Height in the contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>:thumbs up:<br /> <br /> I should clarify I don't hate Ur-Shulgi. I LOVE to hate Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/LoveToHate\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/LoveToHate</a><br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi is everything wrong with V:TM Revised with being an invincible NPC who proceeds to utterly wreck the setting but he's so overthetop and setting breaking that I really enjoy coming up with scenarios that he dies horribly. I've used him multiple times and had various scenarios where the PCs come up with rituals, awakening ancients, and getting the US military to bomb him that gives a real sense of accomplishment to the PCs.<br /> <br /> Like, a good Beckett and PC Indiana Jones-style adventure to find the True Name of Ur-Shulgi and wipe him out.<br /> <br /> Because he's DETESTABLE and ruins the game world if he sticks around but never BORING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-27-2022, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T17:52:25-07:00","id":1488232,"title":"","content":"I really like Jurgen and Gotson from the Dark Ages Novel. As well as Myca Vykos from the same saga, which until then I just found him obnoxious and omnipresent in every GODDAMN story and book, especially in Dark Ages. But I've grown to see him a bit more deep, tragic and jaded to hell.<br /> <br /> I like Vasantasena and Julia Antasia, who are pro-Humanity, but are too different beasts. Unfortunately the latter is forgotten, the former is basically (when it appears) Indian tantrism incarnate as far as I saw. So... unfortunate waste. <br /> <br /> Velya is a pretty cool character too, but the whole grafted girl thing kinda leaned the character to something else.<br /> <br /> Hardestadt is a figure for the ages, but as in-canon, I don't like it. <br /> I like to think him and Rafael de Corazon make a funny sitcom duo.<br /> <br /> Netchurch is a nice change of the &quot;wooowooo I'm nutty&quot; or &quot;hear ye hear ye prophecies mate&quot; Malkavian formula. Even if he unitizing Blood Points was.... 20% cool 80% silly as hell.<br /> <br /> I also love Claudius Giovanni cuz he is such a fucking prick, a Grade-A scheeming bastard. Augustus did well in tearing him apart. <br /> <br /> <br /> I can't remember many modern guys and gals unfortunately. Gary Golden is ... well, unforgettable though.<br /> But the last goes to Mukhtar Bay. A Caitiff Prince in one of the biggest cities, serving as a diplomatic site for sects, for centuries? What a goddamn lad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T18:07:57-07:00","id":1488233,"title":"","content":"Speaking of my favorite NPCs:<br /> <br /> (I fully believe a lot of these will come as no surprise)<br /> <br /> <u>Signature Characters</u><br /> <br /> <b>Lucita</b>: Original Recipe Rebellious Lasombra Princess. She's an archetype and also the closest thing to an Anarch in the Signature Characters, She wants to live free of her sire and be with the ones she loves (Anatole, Fatima, and maybe Beckett). She was done dirty by the Lasombra Trilogy and I blame her being Dominated by the Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> <u>Chicago by Night</u><br /> <br /> <b>Lodin</b>: My original love-to-hate character, I absolutely loved the way the books presented the multi-faceted nature of Chicago's Prince. He's just a DICK. Lodin worked very well as an antagonist because he was a snob, controlling, vicious to his enemies, and an all-round asshole. However, he wasn't STUPID and if you wanted to be a guy who became one of his goons or agents, then he would reward you for it. You could reasonably side with Lodin in a game and even if you were an Anarch or Independent, he was a guy that you might team up with against a potentially greater threat.<br /> <br /> He was a multifacted guy with people he loved, weaknesses, and strengths both. He also wasn't too powerful so that if you wanted to use Lodin as your archnemesis, yes, it would be hard but there was a chance you could take him out. I was saddened by Olaf One Eye because Lodin deserved better. I almost feel like my Anarchs should heal him (probably via diablerizing Cristias) to become who he was.<br /> <br /> <b>Modius</b>: I have a super-soft spot for Modius because he's so damn ludicrous and pathetic but if you take a moment to look at his stats, he's still DANGEROUS. I like the idea that Elders can degenerate so much they become a shadow of themselves and the fact that he's the Prince of Gary, Indiana makes it an interesting &quot;starter villain&quot; scenario. The PCs can overthrow Modius pretty easily if they work at it but that leaves them with Gary. Do they want it? I also like how petty and cruel his manipulations are as well. What he did to Allicia is particularly awful and yet perfect for a vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Allicia</b>: I still love her decades later. The whole &quot;Victorian romance heroine&quot; feel to her and her relationship to Modius worked well for me. I regret they didn't include the offbeat weirdness of her owning the Torch stripclub, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T20:04:49-07:00","id":1488241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488233#post1488233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Allicia</b>: I still love her decades later. The whole &quot;Victorian romance heroine&quot; feel to her and her relationship to Modius worked well for me. I regret they didn't include the offbeat weirdness of her owning the Torch stripclub, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they say she <i>doesn't</i> own said strip club, though? Does anyone else own said club, now? <br /> <br /> What I find odd is no one seems to mention Helena. I'm a Requiem player, so I guess it doesn't matter, but she's a weird one. Is Helena supposed to be a major player or not? Because she's apparently a bloody Fourth Generation who's seen the destruction of Carthage and Pompeii, and the founder of the Succubus Club, for whatever that's worth, but she's also pretending to be a Neonate to hide from the world and barely a Wight.<br /> <br /> What's the deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T23:58:34-07:00","id":1488326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488231#post1488231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ur-Shulgi is everything wrong with V:TM Revised with being an invincible NPC who proceeds to utterly wreck the setting but he's so overthetop and setting breaking that I really enjoy coming up with scenarios that he dies horribly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add to that that he has the personality of a spoon, so destroying him is plenty of fun and we never feel the setting is lessened by his absence.<br /> <br /> Other than being there to be wrecked royally, he very quickly outstayed his welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T00:18:52-07:00","id":1488329,"title":"","content":"Fat Larry. When I accidentally chose the game's hard mode because I thought being a Nosferatu would be cool, Fat Larry showed me acceptance and offered me a mortal's respect.<br /> <br /> I'm his S&amp;M lookin' gremlin; hideous, but cool with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T00:23:17-07:00","id":1488330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488232#post1488232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the last goes to Mukhtar Bay. A Caitiff Prince in one of the biggest cities, serving as a diplomatic site for sects, for centuries? What a goddamn lad</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Mukhtar Bey as well. In my Cairo game he has become a wight and is currently the main villain of the story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T11:48:42-07:00","id":1488373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488241#post1488241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they say she <i>doesn't</i> own said strip club, though? Does anyone else own said club, now?<br /> <br /> Helena still runs The Succubus Club through intermediaries if I recall from the newest version of C.B.N<br /> .<br /> What I find odd is no one seems to mention Helena. I'm a Requiem player, so I guess it doesn't matter, but she's a weird one. Is Helena supposed to be a major player or not? Because she's apparently a bloody Fourth Generation who's seen the destruction of Carthage and Pompeii, and the founder of the Succubus Club, for whatever that's worth, but she's also pretending to be a Neonate to hide from the world and barely a Wight.<br /> <br /> What's the deal?</div> </div> </div> </div>For now she is trying to stave off the beckoning and find a new rival since Menalus of the Brujah has vanished and I guess she is little paraniod of lesser kindred who would want her powerful blood and increase there own power. From what I read of her bio our Helena likes to very behind the scenes in her games and keep people guessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T12:01:12-07:00","id":1488376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488373#post1488373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For now she is trying to stave off the beckoning and find a new rival since Menalus of the Brujah has vanished and I guess she is little paraniod of lesser kindred who would want her powerful blood and increase there own power. From what I read of her bio our Helena likes to very behind the scenes in her games and keep people guessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought she wanted Menele (who in my albiet uninformed opinion, seems a much more interesting character, aside from having TEN Humanity) gone. Why would Helena want someone to replace him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-31-2022, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T12:22:51-07:00","id":1488378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488376#post1488376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought she wanted Menele (who in my albiet unifromed opinion, seems a much more interesting character, aside from having TEN Humanity) gone. Why would Helena want someone to replace him?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Helena has allowed herself to be defined by her rivalry for Menele for much of her immortal existence and can't picture a existence without him or someone like him who could hold her interest and she may find it in the form of Nerissa Blackwater who has a strong dislike for the Toreador. Look at what happened to the Lasombra elder Luciata after her sire Moncada was gone. All her life and unlife she has been defined by her rebellion from a parental figure who wanted her to behave and be a good proper lady. With her biological father and her sire gone and not having Antaole around to ground her as some sort of touchstone, our elder went into a downward spiral and had to join the Sabbat just to stay &quot;sane&quot;.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it you have to wonder if the Helena and Menele really wanted to truly kill each other? They are both powerful enough to have ended it long ago and it brings many sad facets of there type of immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-30-2022, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T16:35:58-07:00","id":1488406,"title":"","content":"Myka/Sascha Vykos, because while I am not Trans it is the first character I saw in fiction who was as a part of it's identity, not the only reason it is in the story, and the rest of the story was great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T17:37:36-07:00","id":1488418,"title":"","content":"While I have in general little attachment to most characters, I think my favorite one is Meerlinda. Next is a draw between Lambach and Menele. The more a character affects inhumanity, the less interesting they become to me, so many popular characters simply aren't my cup of tea, which curiously includes Vykos (despite recognizing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a>'s praise on them, just don't work for me personally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T17:40:44-07:00","id":1488420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488418#post1488418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I have in general little attachment to most characters, I think my favorite one is Meerlinda. Next is a draw between Lambach and Menele. The more a character affects inhumanity, the less interesting they become to me, so many popular characters simply aren't my cup of tea, which curiously includes Vykos (despite recognizing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a>'s praise on them, just don't work for me personally).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel Vykos' status as one of the early trans characters in the game and most prominent is undercut by the fact they were treated as an inhuman monster until OPP retconned their particular awfulness (versus regular vampire awfulness) into being the Dracon's influence.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T17:54:17-07:00","id":1488422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488420#post1488420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel Vykos' status as one of the early trans characters in the game and most prominent is undercut by the fact they were treated as an inhuman monster until OPP retconned their particular awfulness (versus regular vampire awfulness) into being the Dracon's influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with the retcon there's the general matter of the character conflating transgenderism with transhumanism. While it isn't a forbidden thing to do or anything, adding transhuman themes do water down the transgender themes in the eyes of most people, which has the effect of reducing the impact the character would otherwise have.<br /> <br /> But then, it makes the question more interesting for many people, including many (transgender included) that love transhuman stories and so on. I don't have a definitive position on the matter if it is a good or bad thing in itself. But as I said, doesn't quite work for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T13:47:34-07:00","id":1488489,"title":"","content":"I like them old and powerful. Saulot, Ur- shulgi and then probably Mithras or Michael! Honorably mention to my boy Gustav Breidenstein!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 07-30-2022, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T19:24:05-07:00","id":1488522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488378#post1488378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Helena has allowed herself to be defined by her rivalry for Menele for much of her immortal existence and can't picture a existence without him or someone like him who could hold her interest and she may find it in the form of Nerissa Blackwater who has a strong dislike for the Toreador. Look at what happened to the Lasombra elder Luciata after her sire Moncada was gone. All her life and unlife she has been defined by her rebellion from a parental figure who wanted her to behave and be a good proper lady. With her biological father and her sire gone and not having Antaole around to ground her as some sort of touchstone, our elder went into a downward spiral and had to join the Sabbat just to stay &amp;quot;sane&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it you have to wonder if the Helena and Menele really wanted to truly kill each other? They are both powerful enough to have ended it long ago and it brings many sad facets of there type of immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, that's the way I'm playing them in my Chicago 1991 game. They keep manipulating pawns instead of going for the final blow because deep inside they know their existences would be empty if they won. I don't see them in the opposite end of the humanity spectrum, but both sit at low (2-4) humanity.<br /> And this story is clearly and lovely paralleled by the Payne's, who are actually really cool characters. <br /> I am even playing with the idea that Helena and Melene were lovers for a time in Carthage. After Menele left the city on his mission their bond weakened a lot, but it's still there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:58:42-07:00","id":1488802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488241#post1488241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they say she <i>doesn't</i> own said strip club, though? Does anyone else own said club, now?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st edition Storyteller's Screen there was an adventure during which PCs could get the ownership of this joint. <br /> <br /> My personal favourites (and I generally don't like Malkavians, most people can't create something original using them, either as PC or SPC) are Evan Klein (I love the look of my player's faces when he show his new facet) and a Malkavian from modern scenario for V:tM-R (unfortunately I can't remember his name). I recreated this scenario once as a p&amp;p game. He was afraid of dirt so I made him a great fighter but in the moment he was pulled down on the floor he was defeated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T05:10:53-07:00","id":1488805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487542-your-all-time-favorite-npcs-of-v-tm-and-why?p=1488802#post1488802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 1st edition Storyteller's Screen there was an adventure during which PCs could get the ownership of this joint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had it show up in THE MURDER OF MODIUS.<br /> <br /> Because I always felt it was a weird but interesting quirk for the Gothic heroine archetype.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum